{"id": "a0329f12-c9c1-40ea-81db-5c3733c6b945", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "This is a bounded, multi-source readiness check rather than a root-cause investigation, so it's worth delegating to subagents for efficiency. I'm planning to use the Bedrock security assessment skill to check data retention posture — invocation logging, log retention, S3 retention, guardrails — alongside Service Quotas and CloudWatch usage metrics for quota headroom.

I'll tell the user the plan, then spawn two parallel subagents: one for quota headroom, one for data retention posture, letting each discover accounts/regions via list_associations with us-east-1 as the default.

"}]}

{"id": "0cb59aee-bdd4-489a-8598-2a23760fa7b5", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll check this from two angles at once: Bedrock quota headroom (Service Quotas against actual usage) and data-retention posture (invocation logging, log and S3 retention, encryption, guardrails). I'll combine the findings into a readiness call.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_Zxwm5A27gzU57SKtrLTm0R", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "bedrock-quota-headroom", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["exploring-metrics"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Assess Amazon Bedrock quota headroom for production readiness. Read-only.",
  "context": "User asks 'Are we ready to run Bedrock in production?' Agent space is in account 012345678901_1, region us-east-1; also check other associated accounts/regions where Bedrock is used (use list_associations; check regions where Bedrock model invocation metrics exist, at least us-east-1 and us-west-2). Current time 2026-11-15T22:01:00Z.",
  "resources": ["Service Quotas service code 'bedrock'", "CloudWatch namespaces AWS/Bedrock and AWS/Usage", "Bedrock provisioned throughput, cross-region inference profiles"],
  "timeframe": "Last 14 days, ending 2026-11-15T22:01:00Z",
  "criteria": "1) List the applied Service Quotas for Bedrock that matter in production (on-demand requests per minute and tokens per minute for each model actually in use or enabled, provisioned throughput model units, custom model/import limits, guardrail limits, knowledge base/agent limits). Flag any still at default low values and whether they are adjustable. 2) Compare against actual peak usage from CloudWatch AWS/Bedrock metrics (Invocations, InputTokenCount, OutputTokenCount, InvocationThrottles, InvocationClientErrors/ServerErrors, InvocationLatency) per ModelId; compute peak utilization % of quota and headroom. Note throttles observed. 3) Note which models are actually enabled/used. 4) If Bedrock has no usage or is not enabled, say so clearly. Return a concise table of model/quota, limit, peak usage, headroom %, and a short list of risks and recommended quota increases. Do not attempt any mutating operations."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Check Bedrock quotas versus actual usage"}, {"id": "tooluse_fEigsvBcRsNuiEQHwuiNRf", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "bedrock-retention-posture", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["aiml-bedrock-security-assessment"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Assess Amazon Bedrock data-retention and data-handling posture for production readiness. Read-only.",
  "context": "User asks 'Are we ready to run Bedrock in production?' and wants data-retention posture checked. Agent space is in account 012345678901_1, region us-east-1; also check other associated accounts/regions where Bedrock is used (use list_associations). Current time 2026-11-15T22:01:00Z.",
  "resources": ["Bedrock model invocation logging configuration (get_model_invocation_logging_configuration)", "CloudWatch log groups and S3 buckets receiving Bedrock logs", "Bedrock guardrails, knowledge bases, agents, custom models, KMS keys, VPC endpoints for bedrock-runtime", "CloudTrail trails"],
  "timeframe": "Current state",
  "criteria": "Determine: 1) Is model invocation logging enabled, to where (S3/CloudWatch), are prompts/responses/embeddings/images logged (text/image/embedding delivery flags)? 2) Retention: CloudWatch log group retention period (or never-expire), S3 bucket lifecycle rules, versioning, Object Lock, replication, public access block, encryption (SSE-KMS vs SSE-S3) for log destinations. 3) Encryption of Bedrock resources with CMKs (guardrails, knowledge bases, agents, custom models, S3 data sources, vector stores); KMS key rotation. 4) Guardrail coverage (PII filters/sensitive info, content filters) and whether guardrails exist at all. 5) VPC endpoints (bedrock, bedrock-runtime) and CloudTrail coverage for Bedrock API events. 6) Any knowledge base data/vector store retention concerns (e.g., OpenSearch/Aurora snapshots). Report severity-rated findings (High/Medium/Low), with evidence (resource names, config values) and remediation. Clearly state if Bedrock is not configured/used. Do not attempt any mutating operations."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Check Bedrock logging, retention and encryption posture"}], "created_at": null}

